    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The steps are as follows:\n\n1. Divide 20 by 12 to get a quotient of 1 and a remainder of 8.\n   \\[\n   20 = 12 \\cdot 1 + 8\n   \\]\n2. Now, replace the larger number (20) with the smaller number (12) and the smaller number (12) with the remainder (8), then divide 12 by 8:\n   \\[\n   12 = 8 \\cdot 1 + 4\n   \\]\n3. Again, replace the larger number (12) with the smaller number (8) and the smaller number (8) with the remainder (4), then divide 8 by 4:\n   \\[\n   8 = 4 \\cdot 2 + 0\n   \\]\nSince the remainder is now 0, the last non-zero remainder is the GCD. In this case, the GCD of 12 and 20 is 4. Therefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\boxed{4}.",
