    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm is based on the principle that the GCD of two numbers also divides their difference. The algorithm involves repeated division and taking the remainder until we reach a remainder of 0. The last non-zero remainder is the GCD.\n\nUsing the Euclidean algorithm:\n\n1. 20 = 12 * 1 + 8\n2. 12 = 8 * 1 + 4\n3. 8 = 4 * 2 + 0\n\nThe last non-zero remainder is 4, so the GCD of 12 and 20 is \\boxed{4}.",
